WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.413
Tuist 4.218 brings

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.250
coverage to Rust

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:03.746
crates

00:00:04.278 --> 00:00:06.105
Version 4.218 of

00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:06.836
Tuist is out

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:07.226
today

00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:08.461
The tuist cargo

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:09.664
command now reports

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.454
code coverage

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:11.503
scoped to your

00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:12.423
own crates rather

00:00:12.235 --> 00:00:13.803
than every dependency

00:00:14.326 --> 00:00:15.446
Tuist share can

00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:16.189
now attach an

00:00:16.001 --> 00:00:17.521
icon to executable

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:18.087
previews

00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:19.054
one of four

00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:20.116
changes listed in

00:00:19.927 --> 00:00:20.941
the Tuist release

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:21.578
announcement

00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:22.872
You can sign

00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:23.521
in with workload

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:24.122
identities

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:24.771
so there is

00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.396
no token to

00:00:25.208 --> 00:00:26.587
manage and shard

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:27.707
downloads now resume

00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:28.745
after an interruption

00:00:28.557 --> 00:00:29.629
instead of starting

00:00:29.441 --> 00:00:29.995
over

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.548
Full story on

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:32.255
the dashboard
